# Secrets — env files are injected at runtime by the platform / compose
# (`env_file:`), never copied into the image. Without this, `COPY . .` in
# apps/api/Dockerfile pulls apps/api/.env.production into a layer and the
# credentials stay readable with `docker save` + `tar` (or `docker run
# cat .env`).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Installed and built inside the image (pnpm install / nest build);
# copying the host copies would overwrite them with host-platform files.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/logs
